Subject: [PATCH] fix(jbpf): anchor .gitignore build rule so ck templates are tracked

The unanchored `build` rule in external/jbpf/.gitignore matches at every
level, so it excludes 3p/ck/build/ -- Concurrency Kit's 15 configure input
templates, which are source, not build output. In this repo that directory
is missing entirely, so ./build.sh cannot succeed from a clean clone.

Without the templates ck's configure exits 0 having written a zero-byte
ck.build, ALL_LIBS comes out empty, make reports "Nothing to be done", and
the build fails minutes later somewhere unrelated:

    cp: cannot stat 'src/libck.so': No such file or directory
    make: *** [Makefile:51: install-so] Error 1

Anchoring to /build preserves the original intent (ignore jbpf's own
top-level CMake output directory) and is sufficient on its own:
3p/ck/.gitignore already ignores exactly the five generated files
(build/ck.build, build/ck.pc, build/ck.spec, build/Makefile,
build/regressions.build) while tracking the templates. No new ignore
entries are needed.

After applying, restore the 15 templates from ck 0.7.1 and commit them:

    git add -A external/jbpf/3p/ck/build     # 15 files, generated ones stay ignored
    git commit

Verify with:

    git ls-files external/jbpf/3p/ck/build | wc -l    # expect 15

--- a/external/jbpf/.gitignore
+++ b/external/jbpf/.gitignore
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 *.o
 *~
 *.pyc
-build
+/build
 debug_output.txt
 *.tmp
 helper_build_files/symver.map
